# Product Requirements Document (PRD): Loan User Management React Frontend

## 1. Overview

The Loan User Management React Frontend is a web application that provides a user-friendly interface for interacting with the Loan User Management Microservice. This frontend will allow users to perform all operations available in the backend API through an intuitive and responsive UI.

## 2. Objectives

- Create a modern, responsive React application for loan user management
- Implement all functionality available in the backend microservice
- Provide intuitive user interfaces for managing users and loans
- Enable easy visualization of user-loan relationships
- Support all CRUD operations for both users and loans
- Display user OOO status and enable filtering based on status
- Allow for loan transfers between users
- Implement an efficient and user-friendly dashboard

## 3. Functional Requirements

### 3.1 User Management
- View a list of all users with pagination and filtering options
- View detailed information about a specific user
- Create new users with all required information and OOO status
- Update existing user information including OOO status
- Delete users with confirmation
- Search for users by various criteria
- View user count statistics
- Visual indicator for users with OOO status

### 3.2 Loan Management
- View a list of all loans with pagination and filtering options
- View detailed information about a specific loan
- Create new loans with all required details
- Associate loans with specific users during creation or update
- Update existing loan information
- Delete loans with confirmation
- Search for loans by various criteria
- View loan count statistics

### 3.3 User-Loan Relationship
- View all loans associated with a selected user
- Add new loans to a user
- Transfer loans between users with an intuitive interface
- Visualize loan distribution among users

### 3.4 Dashboard
- Overview of system statistics (total users, total loans, active loans, etc.)
- Quick access to users with OOO status
- Recent activity log
- Performance metrics visualization

## 4. Technical Requirements

### 4.1 Architecture
- Single-page application (SPA) using React
- State management with Redux or Context API
- REST API integration with the backend microservice
- Responsive design for various screen sizes

### 4.2 Technology Stack
- React 18+ with functional components and hooks
- TypeScript for type safety
- Redux Toolkit or React Context API for state management
- React Router for navigation
- Axios for API calls
- Material-UI or Ant Design for UI components
- Chart.js or D3.js for data visualization
- React Testing Library and Jest for testing

### 4.3 Key UI Components

**Layout Components:**
- Navigation bar with quick access to main features
- Sidebar for detailed navigation
- Footer with system information
- Responsive container layout

**User Management Components:**
- User list with pagination, sorting, and filtering
- User detail view/form
- User creation/edit form
- User search component
- OOO status toggle with visual indicators

**Loan Management Components:**
- Loan list with pagination, sorting, and filtering
- Loan detail view/form
- Loan creation/edit form
- Loan search component
- Loan status indicators

**User-Loan Components:**
- User loans view
- Loan assignment interface
- Loan transfer interface
- User-loan relationship visualization

**Dashboard Components:**
- Statistics cards
- Activity timeline
- Data visualization charts
- Quick action buttons

## 5. UI/UX Requirements

### 5.1 User Interface
- Clean, modern interface with consistent styling
- Intuitive navigation with breadcrumbs
- Responsive design that works on desktop, tablet, and mobile
- Consistent color scheme and typography
- Clear visual hierarchy
- Accessibility compliance (WCAG 2.1 AA)

### 5.2 User Experience
- Minimal loading times and optimized performance
- Meaningful loading indicators
- Clear feedback for all user actions
- Form validation with helpful error messages
- Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions
- Persistent user preferences
- Keyboard navigation support

## 6. Application Flows

### 6.1 User Management Flow
1. View list of users
2. Filter/search for specific users
3. View user details
4. Create/edit/delete users
5. Toggle OOO status

### 6.2 Loan Management Flow
1. View list of loans
2. Filter/search for specific loans
3. View loan details
4. Create/edit/delete loans

### 6.3 Loan Transfer Flow
1. Select source user
2. View loans assigned to source user
3. Select loans to transfer
4. Select target user
5. Confirm and complete transfer

## 7. API Integration

The frontend will integrate with all endpoints from the backend microservice:

### 7.1 User API Integration
- Implement all user-related API calls
- Handle success and error responses appropriately
- Implement caching for frequently accessed user data

### 7.2 Loan API Integration
- Implement all loan-related API calls
- Handle success and error responses appropriately
- Implement caching for frequently accessed loan data

### 7.3 User-Loan API Integration
- Implement all user-loan relationship API calls
- Enable seamless loan transfers

## 8. Non-Functional Requirements

### 8.1 Performance
- Initial load time under 2 seconds
- Response time for user interactions under 300ms
- Efficient network requests with appropriate caching
- Optimized bundle size

### 8.2 Security
- Input validation on all forms
- CSRF protection
- Secure API communication
- XSS prevention

### 8.3 Maintainability
- Well-structured component hierarchy
- Consistent coding style and documentation
- Reusable components
- Comprehensive test coverage

## 9. Testing Requirements

- Unit tests for all components
- Integration tests for component interactions
- End-to-end tests for critical user flows
- Accessibility testing
- Cross-browser testing
- Responsive design testing

## 10. Acceptance Criteria

- All screens and flows function as specified
- UI is responsive across different device sizes
- All API integrations function correctly
- Forms include proper validation
- Users can perform all CRUD operations on both users and loans
- Loan transfer functionality works as specified
- OOO status is clearly visible and can be toggled
- Dashboard presents relevant information
- Application meets performance requirements

## 11. Future Enhancements

- Advanced filtering and reporting capabilities
- Data export functionality
- User activity logs
- Role-based access control
- Dark mode support
- Internationalization support